 ============================================================
📂 Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) Concepts in Python
 ============================================================
Points that we covered...........
 1. Class:
#    - Blueprint for creating objects.
#    - Defines attributes (variables) and methods (functions).
#
 2. Object:
#    - Instance of a class.
#    - Represents real-world entities with state (attributes) and behavior (methods).

 3. Encapsulation:
#    - Bundling data and methods together.
#    - Restricting direct access using private/protected members.
#    - Achieved via naming conventions (_protected, __private).

 4. Abstraction:
#    - Hiding implementation details, exposing only essentials.
#    - Achieved using abstract classes and methods (abc module).

 5. Inheritance:
#    - Mechanism to reuse code by deriving new classes from existing ones.
#    - Types: Single, Multiple, Multilevel, Hierarchical, Hybrid.

 6. Polymorphism:
#    - Same interface, different implementations.
#    - Method Overriding (runtime polymorphism).
#    - Method Overloading (not natively supported, but can be mimicked).

 7. Constructor (__init__):
#    - Special method to initialize object attributes.

 8. Destructor (__del__):
#    - Special method to clean up resources when object is deleted
